Pipeline variants against the live render pass.

D3D12 lets a pipeline carry more colour targets than the pass binds (writes to unbound targets are discarded), a
pipeline without a depth format draw with a depth buffer bound (the buffer is ignored), a pipeline's colour format
differ from the target's, and a triangle pipeline draw lines or points under dynamic topology; Metal's validation
calls each undefined, vkd3d-proton emits them all for Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024, and Apple GPUs hang on some.
At bind time the graphics pipeline compares its Metal descriptor with the live subpass (colour slots, depth,
stencil) and the drawn primitive class and, when they differ, builds and caches a variant of its pipeline state
against the pass's formats and the drawn class (a colour slot the pass lacks becomes Invalid with blending off, a
slot whose format differs takes the pass's format, depth and stencil take the pass's, the class the draw's); the
base state stays when a variant fails to build (logged). The descriptor copy a variant needs is kept for the
pipeline's life: a form that released it at the first bind whose pass matched lost the variants for exactly the
pipelines that switch targets (a fullscreen pipeline first drawn on an RGBA16F pass, then on the RGBA8 swapchain
pass with depth). HB_MVK_PASS_VARIANTS=0 makes no copy and no variants. The declared primitive class stays as
MoltenVK sets it: Metal refuses a pipeline whose vertex shader writes the layer index without one (an earlier form
left it unspecified and lost 114,039 pipelines a flight). useResource skips a nil resource. Measured on the M4 on
2026-10-16 (private/notes/msfs-2024-arm64-boot-2026-10-15.md).

